xnu 0481: premap the wifi pins before touch takes the tlmm block

Measured 2026-11-26 (0480 boot): the probe block now completes (`eUSB2 done`,
`probe done`, `MONDR USB: running`, `MONDRIAN BTTTY`) and the worker starts, but
it stops right after `early GCC 0x62008` -- the next call is `wifi_map_pins()`,
and touch has already mapped the TLMM block. A later `ml_io_map()` of a page
that is already mapped hangs the mapper; the same seven pages mapped before
touch (0475) complete.

The pin premap returns to the top of `mondrian_wifi_premap()`, now that `0480`
guards the eUSB2 PHY writes that used to make this ordering look unsafe. The
worker keeps its late start, so nothing maps beside it.
diff --git a/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c b/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
index d300a39..869c718 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
@@ -2313,6 +2313,13 @@ mondrian_wifi_premap(void)
 	    enabled != 1) {
 		return;
 	}
+	/*
+	 * The pin pages must be taken here, before touch maps the TLMM block:
+	 * a later ml_io_map() of a page that is already mapped hangs the
+	 * mapper (measured 2026-11-26: the worker stopped at `W4 premap pins`
+	 * and `early GCC` when it mapped them after the probe block).
+	 */
+	mondrian_wifi_premap_pins();
 	(void)wifi_map_once(&wifi_bar, WIFI_BAR_BASE, WIFI_BAR_MAP);
 	(void)wifi_map_once(&wifi_parf, WIFI_PARF_PA, WIFI_PARF_SIZE);
 	(void)wifi_map_once(&wifi_phy, WIFI_PHY_PA, WIFI_PHY_SIZE);
